WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.140
[VOCALIZING]

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:04.556
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:04.556 --> 00:00:07.090
(SINGING) Freedom to love--

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:10.570
In this class, I want to share
with you my writing process

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.700
and what comprises a song.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.420
(SINGING) Go down,
Moses, way down,

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:20.230
Moses, go down to every land.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:22.480
When I start a song,
most of my songs

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.130
start with a mumble
track, and what

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.290
I'm doing- the only
thing I'm worried about

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.570
is the melody and the
structure of the song.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:33.190
The bridge is like
more rapid fire lyrics,

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:37.270
building tension, and then
landing again at our chorus.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:41.340
[PLAYING PIANO]

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.980
I just wrote a brand
new song called, "Free."

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.270
I start with the melody--

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.060
[VOCALIZING]

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:51.120
(SINGING) Let it wash
through the valley, soar

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.010
to the mountains, fall
in the deepest blue sea.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:01:00.090
What unique thing do you want
to put out into the world?

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:03.120
Whether you want to make a
moment or start a movement,

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.800
this song writing
class is for you.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.140
(SINGING) We'll see.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:14.270
Rain down freedom, rain
down 'til we're all free.

